        "original_id": "00021ac1-d10d-57a2-8aa8-390268f93fdb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Hawks, Arthur Berthelet, Barry Fitzgerald, Katharine Hepburn, Cary Grant\n- Films: Bringing Up Baby, The Long Voyage Home, How Green Was My Valley, None but the Lonely Heart, The Quiet Man\n- Companies: RKO Radio Pictures\n- Roles: film director, producer, screenwriter, actor\n- Topics: classic Hollywood era, silent movies, stage plays, Broadway, screwball comedy\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Berthelet (1879–1949) was an American film director who moved from directing stage plays, including several on Broadway, to directing silent movies.\n- Howard Hawks (May 30, 1896–December 26, 1977) was an American film director, producer, and screenwriter of the classic Hollywood era.\n- Bringing Up Baby is a 1938 American screwball comedy film directed by Howard Hawks, starring Katharine Hepburn and Cary Grant, and released by RKO Radio Pictures.\n- Barry Fitzgerald had a career spanning almost forty years and appeared in Bringing Up Baby (1938), The Long Voyage Home (1940), How Green Was My Valley (1941), None but the Lonely Heart (1944), and The Quiet Man (1952).",
